            "start_line": 161,
            "end_line": 164,
            "line_count": 4,
            "preview": "for (int year = -200; year < 200; year++) { // Obtain January 1st of the given proleptic year via day-of-year index 1 BritishCutoverDate firstDayOfYear = BritishCutoverChronology.INSTANCE.dateYearDay(year, 1);"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 166,
            "end_line": 168,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Proleptic year 0 and below map to the BC era; year 1 and above map to AD JulianEra expectedEra = (year <= 0) ? JulianEra.BC : JulianEra.AD; assertEquals(expectedEra, firstDayOfYear.getEra());"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 170,
            "end_line": 172,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// BC year-of-era counts upward from 1 as years go back: year 0 → BC 1, year -1 → BC 2, … int yearOfEra = (year <= 0) ? 1 - year : year; assertEquals(yearOfEra, firstDayOfYear.get(YEAR_OF_ERA));"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 174,
            "end_line": 177,
            "line_count": 4,
            "preview": "// Constructing the same date via (era, year-of-era, dayOfYear) must yield an equal date BritishCutoverDate eraBasedDate = BritishCutoverChronology.INSTANCE.dateYearDay(expectedEra, yearOfEra, 1); assertEquals(firstDayOfYear, eraBasedDate);"
          }
        ],
